        {
          "key": "ShortcutActivatedEvent",
          "kind": "variant",
          "doc": {
            "summary": "Event emitted when a keyboard shortcut is activated.",
            "details": "This event is emitted when a registered keyboard shortcut is triggered by the user pressing the corresponding key combination. The event is emitted before the shortcut's callback is invoked, allowing listeners to perform additional actions or logging.\n\n**Example**\n\n```cpp\nauto& manager = ShortcutManager::GetInstance();\n\n// Listen for shortcut activations\nmanager.AddListener<ShortcutActivatedEvent>([](const ShortcutActivatedEvent& event) {\n    std::cout << \"Shortcut activated: \" << event.GetAccelerator() << std::endl;\n    std::cout << \"Shortcut ID: \" << event.GetShortcutId() << std::endl;\n});\n\n// Register a shortcut\nauto shortcut = manager.Register(\"Ctrl+Shift+Q\", []() {\n    std::cout << \"Quick action!\" << std::endl;\n});\n```"
          },
          "signatures": {
